There are two types of cleaning agents out there: sustainable laundry detergent and the chemicals that make it happen.

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{\textit{Sustainability}} -- claims about recycling percentages, plant-based formulas, or zero-waste packaging.
    \item \textbf{\textit{Transistors}} -- the essential electronic component that enables modern electronics, which includes washing machines.
    \item \textbf{\textit{Recyclables}} -- items designed to be reused or processed rather than discarded after a single cycle.
    \item \textbf{\textit{PFAS}} -- increasingly discussed in environmental contexts as associated health concerns (though most research remains inconclusive).
\end{itemize}

\section{Why We Need to Talk About It}

While we celebrate the convenience of powders and liquid sprays, the reality of using them is heavier than you might think.

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{\textit{Health Risks}} -- the widespread presence of high-level contaminants in household products has raised alarms among health organizations.
