**Problem Statement:** Bypassing input validation and WAF rules is a common exploitation technique. In systems where input validation and web application firewalls are deactivated, this allows attackers to inject arbitrary JavaScript, style, and parameters into requests.

**The Vulnerability:** A successful exploitation can lead to arbitrary code execution, session hijacking, or session hijacking by injecting arbitrary JavaScript, style, or parameters into requests.

**Vulnerable Code Example:**
```
<form action="/resource" method="POST">
    <input type="text" name="username" value="admin"><br>
    <input type="password" name="password"><br>
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{your_secret_token_here}"/><br>
